Write skew -> doctor problem
Suppose a hospital requires at least one doctor on call (on_call = true). Currently, both Alice (id = 1) and Bob (id = 2) are on call. Both try to go off-call simultaneously.
1. Tx A (Alice): SELECT count(*) FROM doctors WHERE on_call = true; → Sees 2.
2. Tx B (Bob): SELECT count(*) FROM doctors WHERE on_call = true; → Sees 2.
3. Tx A (Alice): UPDATE doctors SET on_call = false WHERE id = 1; → COMMIT;
4. Tx B (Bob): UPDATE doctors SET on_call = false WHERE id = 2; → COMMIT;
